---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getLangFromUrl } from '../../i18n/ui';

export function getStaticPaths() {
	return [{ params: { lang: undefined } }, { params: { lang: 'en' } }];
}

const lang = getLangFromUrl(Astro.url);
const pageTitle = lang === 'en' ? 'Charter' : '組織章程';
---

<Layout title={pageTitle}>
	<div class="panel">
		<div class="panel-inner">
			{lang === 'zh' && (<>
<h2>臺灣青少年科學發展協會章程</h2>
			<p><em>內政部114年8月台內團字第1140285860號函准予備查</em></p>

			<h3>第一章　總則</h3>
			<p>第一條　本會名稱為臺灣青少年科學發展協會（以下簡稱本會）。</p>
			<p>第二條　本會為依法設立、非以營利為目的之公益性社會團體，以臺灣青少年科學發展為宗旨。</p>
			<p>第三條　本會之任務如下，並依相關法令規定推動及執行：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>提供台灣青少年公平獲取學術及研究資源的機會。</li>
				<li>促進大專院校學術資源對青少年的開放與流通。</li>
				<li>提升青少年之科學素養及興趣。</li>
				<li>增進青少年對於科學研究工作的認識。</li>
				<li>協助對科學有興趣之青少年得到較好的科學訓練。</li>
				<li>協助參與科學研究之青少年得到較好的研究資源。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第四條　本會之主管機關為內政部，本會之目的事業應受各該事業主管機關之指導、監督。</p>
			<p>第五條　本會以全國行政區域為組織區域。</p>
			<p>第六條　本會會址設於主管機關所轄地區，並得報經主管機關核准設分支機構。前項分支機構組織簡則經會員（會員代表）大會通過，報請主管機關核准後行之。會址及分支機構之地址於設置及變更時，應函報主管機關核備。</p>

			<h3>第二章　會員、理事及監事</h3>
			<p>第七條　本會會員及會費分類如下：</p>
			<ul>
				<li>個人會員：凡贊同本會宗旨、具有投入熱忱者，填具入會申請書，經理事會審查通過，並繳納會費後，為個人會員；入會費新臺幣五百元，於會員入會時繳納；常年會費一千元。</li>
				<li>學生會員：未滿25歲以下，具學生身分，凡贊同本會宗旨、具有投入熱忱者，填具入會申請書，經理事會審查通過，並繳納會費後，為學生會員；入會費新臺幣二百元，於會員入會時繳納；常年會費五百元。</li>
				<li>教師會員：持中華民國教師證者，凡贊同本會宗旨、具有投入熱忱者，填具入會申請書，經理事會審查通過，並繳納會費後，為學生會員；入會費新臺幣四百元，於會員入會時繳納；常年會費八百元。</li>
				<li>團體會員：凡贊同本會宗旨之機構或團體，填具入會申請書，經理事會審查通過，並繳納會費後，為團體會員，團體會員推派代表1人，以行使會員權利；入會費新臺幣五千元，於會員入會時繳納；常年會費一萬元。</li>
				<li>贊助會員：凡贊同本會宗旨且贊助本會經費、資源之個人或團體，填具入會申請書，經理事會審查通過後，為贊助會員。</li>
			</ul>
			<p>第八條　會員（會員代表）有表決權、選舉權、被選舉權與罷免權。每一會員（會員代表）為一權。贊助會員無前項權利。</p>
			<p>第九條　本會理事及監事，任期4年。</p>
			<p>第十條　本會置理事9人（含常務理事3人，其中1人為理事長）、候補理事2人。常務理事，由全體理事互選之。理事長，由全體理事就常務理事中選舉之。</p>
			<p>第十一條　本會置監事3人（其中1人為常務監事）、候補監事1人。監事會置常務監事，由監事互選之，監察日常會務，並擔任監事會主席。</p>
			<p>第十二條　會員有遵守本會章程、決議及繳納會費之義務。會員未繳納會費者，不得享有會員權利，連續3年未繳納會費者，視為自動退會。會員經出會、退會或停權處分，如欲申請復會或復權時，除有正當理由經理事會審核通過者外，應繳清前所積欠之會費。</p>
			<p>第十三條　會員（會員代表）有違反法令、章程或不遵守會員大會決議時，得經理事會決議，予以警告或停權處分，其危害團體情節重大者，得經會員大會決議予以除名。</p>
			<p>第十四條　會員有下列情事之一者，為出會：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>死亡。</li>
				<li>喪失會員資格者。</li>
				<li>經會員（會員代表）大會決議除名者。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第十五條　會員得以書面敘明理由向本會聲明退會。</p>

			<h3>第三章　組織及職權</h3>
			<p>第十六條　本會以會員大會為最高權力機構。會員（會員代表）人數超過300人以上者，得分區比例選出會員代表，再合開會員代表大會，行使會員大會職權。會員代表任期與理事、監事相同，其名額及選舉辦法由理事會通過後實施，並報主管機關備查。</p>
			<p>第十七條　會員（會員代表）大會之職權如下：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>訂定與變更章程。</li>
				<li>選舉及罷免理事、監事。</li>
				<li>議決入會費、常年會費、事業費及會員捐款之數額及方式。</li>
				<li>議決年度工作計畫、報告及預算、決算。</li>
				<li>議決會員（會員代表）之除名處分。</li>
				<li>議決財產之買賣、轉讓或他項權利設定等處分。</li>
				<li>議決本會之解散。</li>
				<li>議決與會員權利義務有關之其他重大事項。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>前項第八款重大事項之範圍由理事會定之。</p>
			<p>第十八條　本會理事、監事，由會員（會員代表）選舉之，分別成立理事會、監事會。選舉前項理事、監事時，依計票情形得同時選出候補理事，候補監事，遇理事、監事出缺時，分別依序遞補之。理事會得提出下屆理事、監事候選人參考名單。理事、監事得採用通訊選舉。通訊選舉辦法由理事會通過後實施，並報主管機關備查。</p>
			<p>第十九條　理事長對內綜理督導會務，對外代表本會，並擔任會員大會、理事會主席。理事長因事不能執行職務時，應指定常務理事1人代理之，未指定或不能指定時，由常務理事互推1人代理之。理事長、常務理事出缺時，應於1個月內補選之。</p>
			<p>第二十條　理事會之職權如下：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>審定會員（會員代表）之資格。</li>
				<li>選舉及罷免常務理事、理事長。</li>
				<li>議決理事、常務理事及理事長之辭職。</li>
				<li>聘免工作人員。</li>
				<li>擬訂年度工作計畫、報告及預算、決算。</li>
				<li>得提出下屆理事、監事候選人參考名單。</li>
				<li>其他應執行事項。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第二十一條　常務監事因事不能執行職務時，應指定監事1人代理之，未指定或不能指定時，由監事互推1人代理之。監事會主席（常務監事）出缺時，應於1個月內補選之。</p>
			<p>第二十二條　監事會之職權如下：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>監察理事會工作之執行。</li>
				<li>審核年度決算。</li>
				<li>選舉及罷免常務監事。</li>
				<li>議決監事及常務監事之辭職。</li>
				<li>其他應監察事項。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第二十三條　理事、監事均為無給職，連選得連任。理事、監事之任期自召開本屆第1次理事會之日起計算。</p>
			<p>第二十四條　理事、監事有下列情事之一者，應即解任：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>喪失會員（會員代表）資格者。</li>
				<li>因故辭職經理事會或監事會決議通過者。</li>
				<li>被罷免或撤免者。</li>
				<li>受停權處分期間逾任期二分之一者。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第二十五條　本會置秘書長1人，承理事長之命處理本會事務，其他工作人員若干人，提經理事會通過後聘免之。前項工作人員不得由理事、監事擔任。工作人員權責及分層負責事項由理事會另定之。</p>
			<p>第二十六條　本會得設各種委員會、小組或其他內部作業組織，其組織簡則經理事會通過後施行，變更時亦同。</p>
			<p>第二十七條　本會得由理事會聘請名譽理事長1人，名譽理事、顧問若干人，其聘期與理事、監事之任期同。</p>

			<h3>第四章　會議</h3>
			<p>第二十八條　會員（會員代表）大會分定期會議與臨時會議2種，由理事長召集之，召集時除緊急事故之臨時會議外，應於15日前通知全體應出席人員。定期會議每年召開1次，臨時會議於理事會認為必要，或經會員（會員代表）五分之一以上之請求，或監事會函請召集時召開之。本會辦理法人登記後，臨時會議經會員（會員代表）十分之一以上之請求召開之。會員（會員代表）大會得以視訊會議或其他經中央主管機關公告之方式召集之，簽到及表決方式則配合電子化設備功能辦理。但涉及選舉、補選、罷免事項，應以實體集會方式辦理。</p>
			<p>第二十九條　會員（會員代表）不能親自出席會員大會時，得以書面委託其他會員（會員代表）代理，每1會員（會員代表）以代理1人為限。</p>
			<p>第三十條　會員（會員代表）大會之決議，以會員（會員代表）過半數之出席，出席人數過半數或較多數之同意行之。但下列事項之決議以出席人數三分之二以上同意行之：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>章程之訂定與變更。</li>
				<li>會員（會員代表）之除名。</li>
				<li>理事、監事之罷免。</li>
				<li>財產之處分。</li>
				<li>本會之解散。</li>
				<li>其他與會員權利義務有關之重大事項。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>本會辦理法人登記後，章程之變更以出席人數四分之三以上之同意或全體會員三分之二以上書面之同意行之；本會之解散，得隨時以全體會員三分之二以上之可決解散之。</p>
			<p>第三十一條　理事會每6個月至少舉行會議1次，監事會每6個月至少舉行會議1次，必要時得召開聯席會議或臨時會議。前項會議召集時除臨時會議外，應於7日前通知全體應出席人員，會議之決議，各以理事、監事過半數之出席，出席人數較多數之同意行之。</p>
			<p>第三十二條　理事應出席理事會議，監事應出席監事會議，理事會、監事會不得委託出席。理事會議、監事會議及理監事聯席會議得以視訊會議或其他經中央主管機關公告之方式召集之，理事、監事出席各視訊會議，視為親自出席，簽到及表決方式則配合電子化設備功能辦理。但涉及選舉、補選、罷免事項，應以實體集會方式辦理。理事、監事連續2次無故缺席理事會、監事會者，視同辭職。</p>

			<h3>第五章　經費及會計</h3>
			<p>第三十三條　本會經費來源如下：</p>
			<ol>
				<li>入會費。</li>
				<li>常年會費。</li>
				<li>事業費。</li>
				<li>會員捐款。</li>
				<li>委託收益。</li>
				<li>基金及其孳息。</li>
				<li>其他收入。</li>
			</ol>
			<p>第三十四條　本會會計年度以曆年為準，自每年1月1日起至12月31日止。本會於會計年度開始前由理事會編造年度工作計畫及收支預算表，並於年度終了後3個月內由理事會編造上年度工作報告及會計報告，送監事會審核後造具審核意見書送還理事會，連同當年度工作計畫及收支預算表，提經會員（會員代表）大會通過後報主管機關備查。會員（會員代表）大會因故未能如期召開，可先經本會理事會及監事會或理監事聯席會議通過，事後提報大會追認後，再報請主管機關備查。</p>
			<p>第三十五條　本會於解散後，剩餘財產歸屬所在地之地方自治團體或主管機關指定之機關團體所有。本會解散之清算人選任及財產清算程序，如本會經法人登記，除法律另有規定外，依民法之規定辦理；如本會未經法人登記，應依會員（會員代表）大會決議辦理，會員（會員代表）大會無法決議時，由理事長擔任清算人，並準用民法清算之規定。</p>

			<h3>第六章　附則</h3>
			<p>第三十六條　本章程未規定事項，悉依有關法令規定辦理。</p>
			<p>第三十七條　本章程經會員（會員代表）大會通過後施行，並報主管機關核備，變更時亦同。</p>
			<p>第三十八條　本章程經本會114年10月4日第一屆第一次會員大會通過。</p>
</>)}
{lang === 'en' && (<>
<h2>Charter of the Taiwan Young Science Development Association</h2>
<p><em>Filed for reference by the Ministry of the Interior (Letter Tai-Nei-Tuan-Zi No. 1140285860, August 2025).</em></p>
<p><em>This English text is an unofficial translation for reference only; the Chinese version prevails.</em></p>

<h3>Chapter I　General Provisions</h3>
<p>Article 1　The name of this Association is the Taiwan Young Science Development Association (hereinafter "the Association").</p>
<p>Article 2　The Association is a legally established, non-profit public-interest social organization whose purpose is to promote the scientific development of young people in Taiwan.</p>
<p>Article 3　The tasks of the Association are as follows, to be promoted and carried out in accordance with relevant laws and regulations:</p>
<ol>
	<li>To give young people in Taiwan fair access to academic and research resources.</li>
	<li>To promote the opening and circulation of university academic resources to young people.</li>
	<li>To raise young people's scientific literacy and interest.</li>
	<li>To deepen young people's understanding of scientific research.</li>
	<li>To help young people interested in science receive better scientific training.</li>
	<li>To help young people engaged in scientific research obtain better research resources.</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 4　The competent authority of the Association is the Ministry of the Interior; the Association's activities are subject to the guidance and supervision of the respective competent authorities of those activities.</p>
<p>Article 5　The Association's organizational area is the entire national administrative territory.</p>
<p>Article 6　The Association's address shall be located within the jurisdiction of the competent authority, and branches may be established with the approval of the competent authority. The organizational rules of such branches shall take effect after being adopted by the general assembly of members (member representatives) and approved by the competent authority. The addresses of the Association and its branches shall be reported to the competent authority for record upon establishment and upon any change.</p>

<h3>Chapter II　Members, Directors and Supervisors</h3>
<p>Article 7　The members of the Association and membership dues are classified as follows:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Individual members: Anyone who endorses the Association's purpose and is enthusiastic about contributing, completes an application form, is approved by the board of directors after review, and pays the dues becomes an individual member; entrance fee NT$500, paid upon joining; annual dues NT$1,000.</li>
	<li>Student members: Persons under 25 years of age with student status who endorse the Association's purpose and are enthusiastic about contributing, complete an application form, are approved by the board of directors after review, and pay the dues become student members; entrance fee NT$200, paid upon joining; annual dues NT$500.</li>
	<li>Teacher members: Holders of a Republic of China teacher's certificate who endorse the Association's purpose and are enthusiastic about contributing, complete an application form, are approved by the board of directors after review, and pay the dues become teacher members; entrance fee NT$400, paid upon joining; annual dues NT$800.</li>
	<li>Group members: Any institution or organization that endorses the Association's purpose, completes an application form, is approved by the board of directors after review, and pays the dues becomes a group member; a group member appoints one representative to exercise membership rights; entrance fee NT$5,000, paid upon joining; annual dues NT$10,000.</li>
	<li>Supporting members: Individuals or organizations that endorse the Association's purpose and provide funding or resources to it, complete an application form, and are approved by the board of directors after review become supporting members.</li>
</ul>
<p>Article 8　Members (member representatives) have the right to vote, to elect, to be elected and to recall. Each member (member representative) has one vote. Supporting members do not have the rights stated in the preceding paragraph.</p>
<p>Article 9　The directors and supervisors of the Association serve a term of 4 years.</p>
<p>Article 10　The Association has 9 directors (including 3 executive directors, one of whom is the Chair) and 2 alternate directors. The executive directors are elected by the directors from among themselves. The Chair is elected by all directors from among the executive directors.</p>
<p>Article 11　The Association has 3 supervisors (one of whom is the executive supervisor) and 1 alternate supervisor. The board of supervisors has an executive supervisor, elected by the supervisors from among themselves, who oversees day-to-day affairs and serves as chair of the board of supervisors.</p>
<p>Article 12　Members have the duty to abide by the Association's charter and resolutions and to pay membership dues. A member who has not paid dues may not enjoy membership rights; a member who has not paid dues for 3 consecutive years is deemed to have withdrawn voluntarily. A member who has left, withdrawn or been suspended and who wishes to apply for reinstatement of membership or rights shall pay all previously owed dues, unless there is a justifiable reason approved by the board of directors after review.</p>
<p>Article 13　If a member (member representative) violates laws or the charter, or fails to comply with resolutions of the general assembly, the board of directors may resolve to issue a warning or suspension; if the harm to the Association is serious, the general assembly may resolve to expel the member.</p>
<p>Article 14　A member ceases to be a member in any of the following cases:</p>
<ol>
	<li>Death.</li>
	<li>Loss of membership eligibility.</li>
	<li>Expulsion by resolution of the general assembly of members (member representatives).</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 15　A member may withdraw from the Association by giving written notice stating the reasons.</p>

<h3>Chapter III　Organization and Powers</h3>
<p>Article 16　The general assembly of members is the Association's highest authority. When the number of members (member representatives) exceeds 300, member representatives may be elected proportionally by region and a general assembly of member representatives convened, exercising the powers of the general assembly of members. The term of member representatives is the same as that of directors and supervisors; their number and election rules shall be adopted by the board of directors before taking effect, and reported to the competent authority for record.</p>
<p>Article 17　The powers of the general assembly of members (member representatives) are as follows:</p>
<ol>
	<li>To establish and amend the charter.</li>
	<li>To elect and recall directors and supervisors.</li>
	<li>To resolve the amount and method of entrance fees, annual dues, program fees and member donations.</li>
	<li>To resolve annual work plans, reports, budgets and final accounts.</li>
	<li>To resolve on the expulsion of members (member representatives).</li>
	<li>To resolve on the sale, transfer or creation of other rights over property.</li>
	<li>To resolve on the dissolution of the Association.</li>
	<li>To resolve other major matters concerning members' rights and obligations.</li>
</ol>
<p>The scope of the major matters in item 8 of the preceding paragraph shall be determined by the board of directors.</p>
<p>Article 18　The directors and supervisors of the Association are elected by the members (member representatives), and form the board of directors and the board of supervisors respectively. In electing directors and supervisors, alternate directors and alternate supervisors may be elected at the same time according to the vote count, and shall fill vacancies in order when a director or supervisor position becomes vacant. The board of directors may propose a reference list of candidates for the next term of directors and supervisors. Directors and supervisors may be elected by correspondence voting; the correspondence voting rules shall be adopted by the board of directors before taking effect, and reported to the competent authority for record.</p>
<p>Article 19　The Chair oversees the Association's affairs internally, represents the Association externally, and serves as chair of the general assembly and of the board of directors. When the Chair cannot perform duties for some reason, the Chair shall designate one executive director to act on their behalf; if none is designated or one cannot be designated, the executive directors shall nominate one among themselves to act. When the position of Chair or of an executive director becomes vacant, a by-election shall be held within one month.</p>
<p>Article 20　The powers of the board of directors are as follows:</p>
<ol>
	<li>To review and determine the qualifications of members (member representatives).</li>
	<li>To elect and recall executive directors and the Chair.</li>
	<li>To resolve on the resignations of directors, executive directors and the Chair.</li>
	<li>To hire and dismiss staff.</li>
	<li>To draft annual work plans, reports, budgets and final accounts.</li>
	<li>To propose a reference list of candidates for the next term of directors and supervisors.</li>
	<li>Other matters to be carried out.</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 21　When the executive supervisor cannot perform duties for some reason, they shall designate one supervisor to act on their behalf; if none is designated or one cannot be designated, the supervisors shall nominate one among themselves to act. When the position of chair of the board of supervisors (executive supervisor) becomes vacant, a by-election shall be held within one month.</p>
<p>Article 22　The powers of the board of supervisors are as follows:</p>
<ol>
	<li>To oversee the execution of the work of the board of directors.</li>
	<li>To audit the annual final accounts.</li>
	<li>To elect and recall the executive supervisor.</li>
	<li>To resolve on the resignations of supervisors and the executive supervisor.</li>
	<li>Other matters requiring supervision.</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 23　Directors and supervisors serve without pay and may be re-elected. The term of directors and supervisors begins on the date the first board of directors meeting of the current term is convened.</p>
<p>Article 24　A director or supervisor shall be removed immediately in any of the following cases:</p>
<ol>
	<li>Loss of membership (member representative) status.</li>
	<li>Resignation for cause approved by resolution of the board of directors or the board of supervisors.</li>
	<li>Recall or removal.</li>
	<li>Suspension lasting longer than half of the term of office.</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 25　The Association has one Secretary-General, who handles the Association's affairs under the direction of the Chair, and a number of other staff, who are hired and dismissed after approval by the board of directors. The staff mentioned in the preceding paragraph may not be directors or supervisors. The duties of the staff and the delegation of responsibilities shall be separately established by the board of directors.</p>
<p>Article 26　The Association may establish committees, working groups or other internal operating bodies; their organizational rules take effect after being adopted by the board of directors, and likewise upon amendment.</p>
<p>Article 27　The board of directors may appoint one honorary chair and a number of honorary directors and advisors, whose terms are the same as those of the directors and supervisors.</p>

<h3>Chapter IV　Meetings</h3>
<p>Article 28　General assemblies of members (member representatives) are of two kinds, regular and extraordinary, convened by the Chair; except for extraordinary meetings in an emergency, all persons required to attend shall be notified 15 days in advance. A regular meeting is held once a year; an extraordinary meeting is held when the board of directors deems it necessary, upon request by one fifth or more of the members (member representatives), or upon request by letter from the board of supervisors. After the Association completes juridical-person registration, an extraordinary meeting shall be held upon request by one tenth or more of the members (member representatives). General assemblies of members (member representatives) may be convened by video conference or other methods announced by the central competent authority, with sign-in and voting handled in accordance with the functions of the electronic equipment; however, matters involving elections, by-elections or recalls shall be conducted in person.</p>
<p>Article 29　When a member (member representative) cannot attend the general assembly in person, they may authorize another member (member representative) in writing to act as proxy; each member (member representative) may act as proxy for only one person.</p>
<p>Article 30　Resolutions of the general assembly of members (member representatives) require the attendance of more than half of the members (member representatives) and are adopted with the consent of more than half, or of a plurality, of those present. However, resolutions on the following matters require the consent of two thirds or more of those present:</p>
<ol>
	<li>Establishment and amendment of the charter.</li>
	<li>Expulsion of members (member representatives).</li>
	<li>Recall of directors and supervisors.</li>
	<li>Disposal of property.</li>
	<li>Dissolution of the Association.</li>
	<li>Other major matters concerning members' rights and obligations.</li>
</ol>
<p>After the Association completes juridical-person registration, amendment of the charter requires the consent of three quarters or more of those present, or the written consent of two thirds or more of all members; the Association may be dissolved at any time by a vote of two thirds or more of all members.</p>
<p>Article 31　The board of directors and the board of supervisors shall each meet at least once every 6 months, and joint meetings or extraordinary meetings may be convened when necessary. Except for extraordinary meetings, all persons required to attend shall be notified 7 days in advance; resolutions of each board are adopted with the attendance of more than half of the directors or supervisors, and the consent of a plurality of those present.</p>
<p>Article 32　Directors shall attend meetings of the board of directors and supervisors shall attend meetings of the board of supervisors; attendance by proxy is not permitted for either board. Meetings of the board of directors, the board of supervisors and joint meetings may be convened by video conference or other methods announced by the central competent authority; directors and supervisors attending by video conference are deemed to be attending in person, with sign-in and voting handled in accordance with the functions of the electronic equipment; however, matters involving elections, by-elections or recalls shall be conducted in person. A director or supervisor who is absent from board meetings 2 consecutive times without cause is deemed to have resigned.</p>

<h3>Chapter V　Funds and Accounting</h3>
<p>Article 33　The Association's funds come from the following sources:</p>
<ol>
	<li>Entrance fees.</li>
	<li>Annual dues.</li>
	<li>Program fees.</li>
	<li>Member donations.</li>
	<li>Commissioned income.</li>
	<li>Funds and the interest thereon.</li>
	<li>Other income.</li>
</ol>
<p>Article 34　The Association's fiscal year follows the calendar year, from January 1 to December 31. Before the start of each fiscal year, the board of directors shall prepare the annual work plan and the revenue-and-expenditure budget; within 3 months after the end of the year, the board of directors shall prepare the previous year's work report and accounting report and send them to the board of supervisors for audit, and the board of supervisors shall draw up an audit opinion and return it to the board of directors; together with the current year's work plan and revenue-and-expenditure budget, these shall be submitted to the general assembly of members (member representatives) for adoption and then reported to the competent authority for record. If the general assembly cannot be held on schedule for some reason, they may first be adopted by the board of directors and the board of supervisors, or at a joint meeting, and then submitted to the general assembly for ratification before being reported to the competent authority for record.</p>
<p>Article 35　After the Association's dissolution, its remaining property shall belong to the local self-governing body of its location or to an agency or organization designated by the competent authority. For the appointment of liquidators and the liquidation procedures upon dissolution: if the Association has completed juridical-person registration, they shall be handled in accordance with the Civil Code unless otherwise provided by law; if it has not, they shall be handled according to the resolution of the general assembly of members (member representatives), and if the general assembly cannot reach a resolution, the Chair shall serve as liquidator and the liquidation provisions of the Civil Code shall apply mutatis mutandis.</p>

<h3>Chapter VI　Supplementary Provisions</h3>
<p>Article 36　Matters not provided for in this charter shall be handled in accordance with relevant laws and regulations.</p>
<p>Article 37　This charter takes effect after adoption by the general assembly of members (member representatives) and filing with the competent authority for record; the same applies to amendments.</p>
<p>Article 38　This charter was adopted at the first general assembly of the first term of the Association on October 4, 2025 (ROC year 114).</p>
